2335
01:42:55.470 --> 01:42:57.890
I've had those moments that have happened,

2336
01:42:57.890 --> 01:43:02.890
I've been and I actually remember them fondly,

2337
01:43:04.420 --> 01:43:07.390
but they're not necessarily easy moments or they're scary.

2338
01:43:07.390 --> 01:43:10.520
And your pulse rate goes down and you just like,

2339
01:43:10.520 --> 01:43:12.613
it's very moment-to-moment.

2340
01:43:13.760 --> 01:43:17.300
It's unlike anything else I've ever or felt really.

2341
01:43:17.300 --> 01:43:20.050
So if you were dispatched to Ukraine right now,

2342
01:43:20.050 --> 01:43:23.490
what would the story be that you would be pursuing?

2343
01:43:23.490 --> 01:43:27.480
Like what would provoke your curiosity?

2344
01:43:27.480 --> 01:43:29.120
What's the story that you're not hearing about?

2345
01:43:29.120 --> 01:43:31.960
Rich, I'm no longer a global traveler that-

2346
01:43:31.960 --> 01:43:34.960
You're pushing a stroller and saying, "What's up daddy?"

2347
01:43:34.960 --> 01:43:38.560
I'm saying, "Let's rock and roll gang."

2348
01:43:38.560 --> 01:43:39.740
That's what I do.

2349
01:43:39.740 --> 01:43:42.550
You know what, of all the stories that I've seen come out,

2350
01:43:42.550 --> 01:43:45.730
I think the refugee story probably is the most interesting

2351
01:43:45.730 --> 01:43:49.720
that Sabrina did and like hanging out in that aspect of it.

2352
01:43:49.720 --> 01:43:54.350
I think were I single and not a father right now,

2353
01:43:54.350 --> 01:43:57.410
would I be, since I actually do have the cash

2354
01:43:57.410 --> 01:43:59.380
to go over there, there's been whole periods of time,

2355
01:43:59.380 --> 01:44:02.130
where I couldn't have funded myself, would I do it?

2356
01:44:02.130 --> 01:44:03.690
It's an interesting question.

2357
01:44:03.690 --> 01:44:05.640
Plenty of like doctors are going to Poland

2358
01:44:05.640 --> 01:44:08.847
and trying to help refugees on that side of border.

2359
01:44:09.900 --> 01:44:13.360
I've tended to be the under-reported story guy.

2360
01:44:13.360 --> 01:44:15.300
And so when the whole world goes to Ukraine,

2361
01:44:15.300 --> 01:44:18.140
I probably wouldn't do that because I'm not working.

2362
01:44:18.140 --> 01:44:20.235
I don't have a connection

2363
01:44:20.235 --> 01:44:24.113
to Daily News editors on that level,

2364
01:44:25.030 --> 01:44:28.160
so I typically try to find the under-reported story.

2365
01:44:28.160 --> 01:44:30.740
But I will say this, like seeing what's happening

2366
01:44:32.129 --> 01:44:35.670
in Ukraine and Russia, we are focused on that.

2367
01:44:35.670 --> 01:44:37.838
For many years I covered Burma and Myanmar

2368
01:44:37.838 --> 01:44:39.720
and they've had a military dictatorship.

2369
01:44:39.720 --> 01:44:42.290
They just retook the country, this military did,

2370
01:44:42.290 --> 01:44:44.740
they've crunched down social media,

2371
01:44:44.740 --> 01:44:45.910
you can't get on social media.

2372
01:44:45.910 --> 01:44:48.460
They've kept their foot on the neck

2373
01:44:48.460 --> 01:44:51.023
of the people for generations.

2374
01:44:52.376 --> 01:44:55.153
And we've done business with them.

2375
01:44:55.153 --> 01:44:56.630
EU done business with them,

2376
01:44:56.630 --> 01:44:59.030
Japan's done business with them this whole time.

2377
01:44:59.030 --> 01:45:03.820
So it is interesting when you've covered other places

2378
01:45:03.820 --> 01:45:05.550
that have had similar situations

2379
01:45:05.550 --> 01:45:07.870
and the Burmese fought back, there's been fighting.

2380
01:45:07.870 --> 01:45:09.180
I mean, not just the Burmese,

2381
01:45:09.180 --> 01:45:12.202
but the different ethnic armies in the provinces

2382
01:45:12.202 --> 01:45:15.340
have fought back against this domination

2383
01:45:15.340 --> 01:45:17.310
for generations as well.

2384
01:45:17.310 --> 01:45:21.710
And nobody's given them a bunch of weapons.

2385
01:45:21.710 --> 01:45:26.010
So when you see that, you do wonder, but at the same time,

2386
01:45:26.010 --> 01:45:29.440
like you understand, because Ukraine has actually managed

2387
01:45:29.440 --> 01:45:32.420
to cut through all the divisive, polarized bullshit.

2388
01:45:32.420 --> 01:45:35.080
And the United States, aside

2389
01:45:35.080 --> 01:45:36.950
from people that work at Fox News

2390
01:45:36.950 --> 01:45:40.023
typically agree that Putin is a bad person.

2391
01:45:40.980 --> 01:45:43.080
And that we should be rooting at least for Ukraine.

2392
01:45:43.080 --> 01:45:44.360
That's an accomplishment, yeah.

2393
01:45:44.360 --> 01:45:45.193
Yeah.

2394
01:45:47.631 --> 01:45:49.460
Well, more will be revealed.

2395
01:45:49.460 --> 01:45:50.930
More will be revealed.

2396
01:45:50.930 --> 01:45:55.180
And we'll do our best to bring you our perspective

2397
01:45:55.180 --> 01:45:57.020
if that's what you wanna hear, who knows?

2398
01:45:57.020 --> 01:45:57.853
Yeah.

2399
01:45:57.853 --> 01:46:00.220
Do people wanna hear us talk about Ukraine?

2400
01:46:00.220 --> 01:46:01.053
I don't know.

2401
01:46:01.053 --> 01:46:02.110
I think we just did Ukraine.

2402
01:46:02.110 --> 01:46:03.142
We just did.

2403
01:46:03.142 --> 01:46:05.214
Do you wanna do Ukraine again

2404
01:46:05.214 --> 01:46:07.005
and see if we can do it better?

2405
01:46:07.005 --> 01:46:08.200
(both laughing)

2406
01:46:08.200 --> 01:46:09.380
I'm sure we could.

2407
01:46:09.380 --> 01:46:10.410
Yes.

2408
01:46:10.410 --> 01:46:12.830
All right let's get to the listener question.

2409
01:46:12.830 --> 01:46:14.120
We have three listener questions,

2410
01:46:14.120 --> 01:46:17.790
and they all pivot around one theme for the most part.

2411
01:46:17.790 --> 01:46:20.560
They're all sobriety, it's a sobriety theme.

2412
01:46:20.560 --> 01:46:21.497
It is.

2413
01:46:21.497 --> 01:46:23.603
Before we get into it, let me ask you a quick question.

2414
01:46:24.710 --> 01:46:27.370
What do you think of the psychedelic day spas

2415
01:46:27.370 --> 01:46:28.930
that are proliferating?

2416
01:46:28.930 --> 01:46:30.890
I didn't know that there were such a thing.

2417
01:46:30.890 --> 01:46:32.288
Let's do that story next.

2418
01:46:32.288 --> 01:46:33.121
All right, we can do that next.

2419
01:46:33.121 --> 01:46:34.170
I have lots of thoughts on this.

2420
01:46:34.170 --> 01:46:36.070
Yeah, that's important I think.

2421
01:46:37.010 --> 01:46:38.950
I can't answer that in one or two sentences.

2422
01:46:38.950 --> 01:46:42.270
No, plus that way I can share about my early experience

2423
01:46:42.270 --> 01:46:45.550
in the legalized medical marijuana reporting

2424
01:46:45.550 --> 01:46:46.986
that I was doing years ago.

2425
01:46:46.986 --> 01:46:50.350
I look forward to hearing that, spa, where are these spas?

2426
01:46:50.350 --> 01:46:52.237
Wouldn't you like to know?

2427
01:46:52.237 --> 01:46:53.537
Maybe, I shouldn't know.

2428
01:46:55.040 --> 01:46:57.310
Julie, from Kansas City.

2429
01:46:57.310 --> 01:47:01.320
Hi, Rich and Adam, this is Julie from Kansas City.

2430
01:47:01.320 --> 01:47:03.210
Just wanted to say, "Tusen takk,"

2431
01:47:03.210 --> 01:47:05.870
which is Norwegian for, a thousand thanks

2432
01:47:05.870 --> 01:47:09.300
because that really just expressed the amount

2433
01:47:09.300 --> 01:47:11.640
of gratitude I have for the podcast.

2434
01:47:11.640 --> 01:47:14.120
I wanted to take a brief second,

2435
01:47:14.120 --> 01:47:17.830
just to tell my husband, Drew, of how proud I am

2436
01:47:17.830 --> 01:47:19.900
of him these past handful of years.

2437
01:47:19.900 --> 01:47:22.140
And it's been the greatest joy

2438
01:47:22.140 --> 01:47:25.930
of my life to watch his road to recovery.

2439
01:47:25.930 --> 01:47:29.550
My question is, as our kids are getting older

2440
01:47:29.550 --> 01:47:32.470
and are starting to enter the tween years,

2441
01:47:32.470 --> 01:47:37.470
what are some pointers or advice that you could give us

2442
01:47:37.560 --> 01:47:41.430
for talking about alcoholism, addiction, sobriety,

2443
01:47:41.430 --> 01:47:44.250
and recovery with our children?

2444
01:47:44.250 --> 01:47:48.700
Appreciate you both and hope you have a great day.

2445
01:47:48.700 --> 01:47:49.533
Thank you, Julie.

2446
01:47:49.533 --> 01:47:52.840
It's a great question, it's a really important question.

2447
01:47:52.840 --> 01:47:56.460
Perhaps one of, if not the most important thing

2448
01:47:56.460 --> 01:47:58.570
to be thinking about as a parent,

2449
01:47:58.570 --> 01:48:03.020
as your kids enter these tween and ultimately teenage years.

2450
01:48:03.020 --> 01:48:05.210
I've been through this myself

2451
01:48:05.210 --> 01:48:09.690
and I have lots of opinions about this and thoughts on it.

2452
01:48:09.690 --> 01:48:14.690
I think it's really important to be honest with your kids

2453
01:48:17.815 --> 01:48:20.290
and not communicate to them in the way

2454
01:48:20.290 --> 01:48:21.520
perhaps our parents did,

2455
01:48:21.520 --> 01:48:23.523
where like it's just drugs are bad.

2456
01:48:24.640 --> 01:48:26.190
I don't think that really works

2457
01:48:26.190 --> 01:48:30.330
this idea of making them scared or labeling

2458
01:48:30.330 --> 01:48:34.230
with judgment, what drugs are and what drugs aren't.

2459
01:48:34.230 --> 01:48:35.740
I think it's much more effective,

2460
01:48:35.740 --> 01:48:37.060
especially since it sounds like,

2461
01:48:37.060 --> 01:48:38.380
so Drew, her husband is in recovery.

2462
01:48:38.380 --> 01:48:40.680
It sounds like it, yeah.

2463
01:48:40.680 --> 01:48:42.470
To be transparent about that,

2464
01:48:42.470 --> 01:48:47.470
to talk openly with your kids about your own history

2465
01:48:47.680 --> 01:48:50.963
and Drew's history with drugs and alcohol, I think is key.

2466
01:48:52.960 --> 01:48:55.420
And in that, what I mean by that is

2467
01:48:57.833 --> 01:49:00.160
you can just talk to them like on some level,

2468
01:49:00.160 --> 01:49:01.090
not that they're adults,

2469
01:49:01.090 --> 01:49:03.400
but you can say, look, I understand that

2470
01:49:03.400 --> 01:49:05.460
you're gonna be faced with temptations.

2471
01:49:05.460 --> 01:49:07.140
Other kids are gonna be doing this.

2472
01:49:07.140 --> 01:49:09.312
There is an allure to it.

2473
01:49:09.312 --> 01:49:12.070
You'll be in a situation where you feel like

2474
01:49:12.070 --> 01:49:14.260
if you wanna fit in, you're gonna have to do it.

2475
01:49:14.260 --> 01:49:16.900
And you could talk about like, when I was doing it,

2476
01:49:16.900 --> 01:49:19.010
here's what happened to me and it was great.

2477
01:49:19.010 --> 01:49:20.660
And I had fun and this is,

2478
01:49:20.660 --> 01:49:23.040
you could talk about the positives and the negatives.

2479
01:49:23.040 --> 01:49:25.700
I think the more open and honest you are,

2480
01:49:25.700 --> 01:49:28.200
the more trust you engender with your kids.

2481
01:49:28.200 --> 01:49:30.440
So you tell good stories too.

2482
01:49:30.440 --> 01:49:32.960
I mean, Julie has told crazy stories to our kids

2483
01:49:32.960 --> 01:49:35.440
about like stuff that she did when she was really young,

2484
01:49:35.440 --> 01:49:37.560
like growing up in Alaska.

2485
01:49:37.560 --> 01:49:39.632
Where she got accidentally dosed with acid

2486
01:49:39.632 --> 01:49:42.333
and what happened to her and you can kind of talk about it,

2487
01:49:42.333 --> 01:49:46.560
you can do it with levity is what I'm saying.

2488
01:49:46.560 --> 01:49:48.950
And I think my perspective has always been,

2489
01:49:48.950 --> 01:49:51.840
look here's how it started for me.

2490
01:49:51.840 --> 01:49:53.250
And here's what it did for me.

2491
01:49:53.250 --> 01:49:54.820
And here's how I think in many ways

2492
01:49:54.820 --> 01:49:58.290
it like kind of soothed me or was

2493
01:49:59.200 --> 01:50:01.720
a bandaid to this emotional wound that I had,

2494
01:50:01.720 --> 01:50:03.650
but ultimately I couldn't control it.

2495
01:50:03.650 --> 01:50:05.550
And here's what happened as a result.

2496
01:50:05.550 --> 01:50:07.430
And I've taken my kids to AA meetings

2497
01:50:07.430 --> 01:50:09.490
and they know my whole history

2498
01:50:09.490 --> 01:50:11.910
and all my AA friends, I have lots of a friends.

2499
01:50:11.910 --> 01:50:14.240
They come over to the house, they share.

2500
01:50:14.240 --> 01:50:16.460
Like we're all very open about it.

2501
01:50:16.460 --> 01:50:20.910
And I think it creates an environment of permissibility

2502
01:50:20.910 --> 01:50:23.840
to talk about it, as opposed to it being this voodoo subject

2503
01:50:23.840 --> 01:50:26.552
that everyone tiptoes around and is scared to talk about

2504
01:50:26.552 --> 01:50:30.510
or does it in a very kind of binary reductive way.

2505
01:50:30.510 --> 01:50:32.373
Right, do you think that's

2506
01:50:32.373 --> 01:50:35.410
because it's a foreground conclusion, kids will experiment.

2507
01:50:35.410 --> 01:50:37.470
It's the rare kid that doesn't try something.

2508
01:50:37.470 --> 01:50:39.190
Yeah, they're gonna be exposed to it.

2509
01:50:39.190 --> 01:50:41.620
And if you think otherwise you're delusional, right?

2510
01:50:41.620 --> 01:50:43.910
So this is going on all around you.

2511
01:50:43.910 --> 01:50:46.530
And if you think, my kid's a good kid,

2512
01:50:46.530 --> 01:50:47.520
he would never do that.

2513
01:50:47.520 --> 01:50:49.680
Or this is not happening with my kid.

2514
01:50:49.680 --> 01:50:51.317
Like you're not living in reality.

2515
01:50:51.317 --> 01:50:54.679
Like this is going on all over the place all the time.

2516
01:50:54.679 --> 01:50:58.920
And to the extent that you have a really good grip

2517
01:50:58.920 --> 01:51:02.730
on like what your kid is doing at school all day long,

2518
01:51:02.730 --> 01:51:04.820
like I've learned, and I've seen

2519
01:51:04.820 --> 01:51:07.980
in other people, like they have their own lives outside

2520
01:51:07.980 --> 01:51:09.690
of the at, and they choose

2521
01:51:09.690 --> 01:51:12.180
what to share with you and what not to share with you.

2522
01:51:12.180 --> 01:51:15.170
Which gets to my point about like, keeping that channel

2523
01:51:15.170 --> 01:51:18.020
of communication as open and as honest as possible.

2524
01:51:18.020 --> 01:51:20.470
In my experience, that's absolutely key.

2525
01:51:20.470 --> 01:51:22.140
And if you just villainize drugs

2526
01:51:22.140 --> 01:51:23.810
or you talk down to your kids,

2527
01:51:23.810 --> 01:51:26.190
or you speak about this subject matter

2528
01:51:26.190 --> 01:51:29.630
in a very judgmental tone, then they're not gonna feel safe

2529
01:51:29.630 --> 01:51:32.970
or comfortable coming to you to ask you questions

2530
01:51:32.970 --> 01:51:36.380
about it, or to confess to something that has happened,

2531
01:51:36.380 --> 01:51:39.140
or to ask for advice about what they should do,

2532
01:51:39.140 --> 01:51:40.930
because this kid did that and they were

2533
01:51:40.930 --> 01:51:43.490
in this situation and they didn't know how to behave.

2534
01:51:43.490 --> 01:51:47.770
Plus if he's only been in recovery for a few years

2535
01:51:47.770 --> 01:51:51.670
and they're gonna be tweens, they've already seen stuff.

2536
01:51:51.670 --> 01:51:53.060
Certainly, right?

2537
01:51:53.060 --> 01:51:54.810
And it's sort of like,

2538
01:51:54.810 --> 01:51:57.140
okay, at tweens, like, so how old exactly?

2539
01:51:57.140 --> 01:51:58.280
Like you do have to, like,

2540
01:51:58.280 --> 01:52:00.904
they need to be mature enough to be able to-

2541
01:52:00.904 --> 01:52:01.904
Understand.

2542
01:52:01.904 --> 01:52:05.770
So I'm talking more about 15, around 14, 15.

2543
01:52:05.770 --> 01:52:06.603
You wouldn't start at 11

2544
01:52:06.603 --> 01:52:08.332
or 12, when talking about this staff?

2545
01:52:08.332 --> 01:52:09.430
Well, no, I think it's a different conversation

2546
01:52:09.430 --> 01:52:11.540
at 11 and 12, you can share your experience.

2547
01:52:11.540 --> 01:52:14.670
And I would encourage taking the kids to these AA meetings.

2548
01:52:14.670 --> 01:52:17.190
Like that's they get exposed to,

2549
01:52:17.190 --> 01:52:19.220
they get to absorb kind of the environment.

2550
01:52:19.220 --> 01:52:21.620
And I think when they're

2551
01:52:21.620 --> 01:52:23.550
at open meetings and they see people get up

2552
01:52:23.550 --> 01:52:24.940
and share with a level

2553
01:52:24.940 --> 01:52:27.430
of vulnerability and honesty about their past

2554
01:52:27.430 --> 01:52:29.590
and their mishaps, and their foibles and how they got

2555
01:52:29.590 --> 01:52:32.320
into trouble and how they built their lives back up,

2556
01:52:32.320 --> 01:52:35.310
like that's impactful on a young mind.

2557
01:52:35.310 --> 01:52:38.110
And they can see that rollercoaster ride,

2558
01:52:38.110 --> 01:52:41.330
that drugs and alcohol takes people on.

2559
01:52:41.330 --> 01:52:43.840
And I think also,

2560
01:52:43.840 --> 01:52:45.790
you need to have a healthy appreciation

2561
01:52:47.513 --> 01:52:49.880
for the lack of control, you're gonna be able

2562
01:52:49.880 --> 01:52:51.770
to exert on these kids as they get older.

2563
01:52:51.770 --> 01:52:54.390
Like you have to surrender and accept that,

2564
01:52:54.390 --> 01:52:56.640
you're not gonna be able to dictate their decisions

2565
01:52:56.640 --> 01:53:00.380
when they're at school, like you can't be with them 24/7.

2566
01:53:00.380 --> 01:53:02.140
And these opportunities

2567
01:53:02.140 --> 01:53:05.560
to drink or use are going to present at themselves.

2568
01:53:05.560 --> 01:53:08.040
Your kid is gonna make a choice.

2569
01:53:08.040 --> 01:53:11.600
Quite often, kids make the wrong choice

2570
01:53:11.600 --> 01:53:14.770
and your job is to provide this safe place

2571
01:53:14.770 --> 01:53:17.080
for them to process this.

2572
01:53:17.080 --> 01:53:19.550
I think the kid has to feel like it's their idea.

2573
01:53:19.550 --> 01:53:20.980
Like I wanna talk to my parent

2574
01:53:20.980 --> 01:53:23.070
about this, or I'm gonna choose not

2575
01:53:23.070 --> 01:53:26.640
to use, but it's almost like forming an inception.

2576
01:53:26.640 --> 01:53:30.780
Like you have to create an environment where

2577
01:53:31.770 --> 01:53:34.415
it's conducive to them developing

2578
01:53:34.415 --> 01:53:36.930
like the level of self-efficacy

2579
01:53:36.930 --> 01:53:40.291
and agency in their life, where they're going

2580
01:53:40.291 --> 01:53:44.157
to make that better decision to have the gumption

2581
01:53:44.157 --> 01:53:48.290
and the sense of self

2582
01:53:48.290 --> 01:53:51.730
to be able to say no under social pressure, right?

2583
01:53:51.730 --> 01:53:53.190
Yeah.

2584
01:53:53.190 --> 01:53:55.140
It's tough though, man.

2585
01:53:55.140 --> 01:53:58.130
Self-sufficiency, self-efficacy, self-esteem,

2586
01:53:58.130 --> 01:54:00.040
the more kids feel good about themselves

2587
01:54:00.040 --> 01:54:02.600
and feel like they have a direction in their life,

2588
01:54:02.600 --> 01:54:04.470
they're secure in their social environment.

2589
01:54:04.470 --> 01:54:05.990
They have a belief in their competence

2590
01:54:05.990 --> 01:54:08.990
and hope for their future, the less likely they're gonna be

2591
01:54:08.990 --> 01:54:11.470
to sacrifice those values or desires

2592
01:54:11.470 --> 01:54:15.490
for that social approval in those tricky situations.

2593
01:54:15.490 --> 01:54:19.060
But it's tough, man, this is a tough road ahead,

2594
01:54:19.060 --> 01:54:23.210
all kids go through this deep desire to fit in.

2595
01:54:23.210 --> 01:54:25.990
And this is something that every parent

2596
01:54:25.990 --> 01:54:29.270
is gonna have to confront and navigate with their kids.

2597
01:54:29.270 --> 01:54:30.937
And I think, but I think the parents

2598
01:54:30.937 --> 01:54:33.210
that have the hardest time with it are the ones

2599
01:54:33.210 --> 01:54:35.760
who think they're not gonna have to deal with this.

2600
01:54:35.760 --> 01:54:37.450
Because they've parented in a certain way

2601
01:54:37.450 --> 01:54:38.283
where they're certain

2602
01:54:38.283 --> 01:54:41.160
that their kid is gonna be able to transcend this.

2603
01:54:41.160 --> 01:54:43.830
And those are the ones who have the biggest come ups

2604
01:54:43.830 --> 01:54:45.270
and it comes as such a surprise

2605
01:54:45.270 --> 01:54:47.810
to them because they feel like they did everything

2606
01:54:47.810 --> 01:54:51.390
to prevent it from happening and it happens.

2607
01:54:51.390 --> 01:54:53.050
Even when you do that, this stuff comes off.

2608
01:54:53.050 --> 01:54:55.230
Well, I think it's very clear in life

2609
01:54:55.230 --> 01:54:57.520
that the more certain you are about a certain outcome,

2610
01:54:57.520 --> 01:55:01.230
the more fucked up you're gonna be pretty soon after.

2611
01:55:01.230 --> 01:55:02.063
I know.

2612
01:55:02.063 --> 01:55:03.840
Well, as somebody who's been a parent

2613
01:55:03.840 --> 01:55:07.500
for a minute and has weathered teen years

2614
01:55:07.500 --> 01:55:10.730
and you has young adults now and all that kind of stuff,

2615
01:55:10.730 --> 01:55:13.870
I always sort of chuckle when I meet young parents

2616
01:55:13.870 --> 01:55:15.500
or parents that are kind of in the situation

2617
01:55:15.500 --> 01:55:17.240
that you're in and they're like, here's what we're doing.

2618
01:55:17.240 --> 01:55:19.800
And they have this whole plan, like here's the school.

2619
01:55:19.800 --> 01:55:20.840
And then we're gonna expose the kid

2620
01:55:20.840 --> 01:55:22.350
to this and he's gonna love this.

2621
01:55:22.350 --> 01:55:24.290
And this is what we're gonna plug him into.

2622
01:55:24.290 --> 01:55:25.780
And this is how it's gonna play out.

2623
01:55:25.780 --> 01:55:26.763
And I'm just like,

2624
01:55:26.763 --> 01:55:29.496
"All right, well, we'll see how that goes."

2625
01:55:29.496 --> 01:55:31.260
(both laughing)

2626
01:55:31.260 --> 01:55:32.210
You know what I mean?

2627
01:55:32.210 --> 01:55:33.269
Yeah.

2628
01:55:33.269 --> 01:55:34.300
The more you try to exert

2629
01:55:34.300 --> 01:55:36.840
that control and it comes from a place of love.

2630
01:55:36.840 --> 01:55:39.080
Every parent wants to see their kid flourish

2631
01:55:39.080 --> 01:55:40.762
and they wanna put them

2632
01:55:40.762 --> 01:55:42.230
in those environments and you should be doing all of that,

2633
01:55:42.230 --> 01:55:44.720
but you have to hold these things lightly.

2634
01:55:44.720 --> 01:55:47.100
And kind of detach from your expectations

2635
01:55:47.100 --> 01:55:49.040
and the more you hold onto it,

2636
01:55:49.040 --> 01:55:52.450
the more of a lesson you're in for, I think.

2637
01:55:52.450 --> 01:55:53.659
I think you're right.

2638
01:55:53.659 --> 01:55:56.760
And it's your point about self-esteem being so key,

2639
01:55:56.760 --> 01:55:59.477
doesn't it help a kid's self-esteem when their parents

2640
01:55:59.477 --> 01:56:01.882
are being kind of honest and raw with them?

2641
01:56:01.882 --> 01:56:03.199
'cause it makes them feel like a grownup, right?

2642
01:56:03.199 --> 01:56:05.070
Yeah, I made these mistakes.

2643
01:56:05.070 --> 01:56:07.020
Like I think when parents try to say,

2644
01:56:07.020 --> 01:56:08.460
I'm the ultimate authority.

2645
01:56:08.460 --> 01:56:10.140
And this is right, and this is wrong

2646
01:56:10.140 --> 01:56:11.450
and you have to do this.

2647
01:56:11.450 --> 01:56:13.970
Kids are very astute because they see the dissonance

2648
01:56:13.970 --> 01:56:16.140
between what comes out of a parent's mouth

2649
01:56:16.140 --> 01:56:18.030
and how they actually behave.

2650
01:56:18.030 --> 01:56:21.710
And that means that you need to align your behavior

2651
01:56:21.710 --> 01:56:23.960
with your words, but you also have

2652
01:56:23.960 --> 01:56:27.800
to be honest and transparent about your mistakes

2653
01:56:27.800 --> 01:56:31.170
and things that you had to learn the hard way.

2654
01:56:31.170 --> 01:56:32.921
And I think that creates a relatability

2655
01:56:32.921 --> 01:56:36.680
and a level of trust that is super important here.

2656
01:56:36.680 --> 01:56:41.680
And look, when that situation arises and you find out

2657
01:56:41.870 --> 01:56:45.200
that your kid got drunk at a party or whatever it is,

2658
01:56:45.200 --> 01:56:46.840
you want them to feel like they can

2659
01:56:46.840 --> 01:56:49.270
come and tell you about that and be honest about it.

2660
01:56:49.270 --> 01:56:51.240
And you're not gonna have to catch them in a lie

2661
01:56:51.240 --> 01:56:53.060
or discover it some other way

2662
01:56:53.060 --> 01:56:55.830
because they wouldn't tell you about it.

2663
01:56:55.830 --> 01:56:57.960
That's because the communication is shut down

2664
01:56:57.960 --> 01:57:00.590
and they don't trust you or they don't feel comfortable

2665
01:57:00.590 --> 01:57:01.642
talking to you about this

2666
01:57:01.642 --> 01:57:04.180
because they're afraid they're gonna be judged.

2667
01:57:04.180 --> 01:57:06.640
They could still be sentenced to child labor for a day,

2668
01:57:06.640 --> 01:57:08.870
if you want, I mean, after they got drunk at the party.

2669
01:57:08.870 --> 01:57:11.570
There can be ramifications for this, of course.

2670
01:57:11.570 --> 01:57:12.710
Is child labor okay?

2671
01:57:12.710 --> 01:57:14.940
I mean, I'm new to this, so I just wanna know.

2672
01:57:14.940 --> 01:57:17.440
Yeah, I don't know child labor in what form?

2673
01:57:17.440 --> 01:57:21.964
Like mow the lawn or we're putting you on a plane to-

2674
01:57:21.964 --> 01:57:24.240
Bangladeshi sweat shop.

2675
01:57:24.240 --> 01:57:28.480
Yeah, I would also highly suggest, Julie,

2676
01:57:28.480 --> 01:57:30.410
that you check out if you haven't,

2677
01:57:30.410 --> 01:57:33.030
if you missed it the first time around

2678
01:57:33.030 --> 01:57:35.907
the podcast that I did with Jessica Lahey on her book,

2679
01:57:35.907 --> 01:57:38.717
"The Addiction Inoculation" that's episode 593,

2680
01:57:38.717 --> 01:57:40.740
'cause we talk about all of this stuff.

2681
01:57:40.740 --> 01:57:42.930
And if you haven't read that book yet,

2682
01:57:42.930 --> 01:57:46.020
I would definitely pick that up, she's the boss.

2683
01:57:46.020 --> 01:57:47.130
That was a great question.

2684
01:57:47.130 --> 01:57:49.700
I have to props to Julie from KC.

2685
01:57:49.700 --> 01:57:51.400
I love Kansas City by the way.

2686
01:57:51.400 --> 01:57:52.310
Cool.

2687
01:57:52.310 --> 01:57:53.143
Big fan.

2688
01:57:54.220 --> 01:57:57.687
Back to Kansas, where the scene of "The Day After".

2689
01:57:58.690 --> 01:58:00.079
I think it was Lawrence, Kansas.

2690
01:58:00.079 --> 01:58:00.912
I think it was Lawrence,

2691
01:58:00.912 --> 01:58:02.260
which is not far from Kansas city.

2692
01:58:02.260 --> 01:58:04.240
Believe me if it happened again.

2693
01:58:04.240 --> 01:58:05.900
I just remember there was a swing set.

2694
01:58:05.900 --> 01:58:08.190
I can like there's a empty swing set

2695
01:58:08.190 --> 01:58:10.050
and then the mushroom cloud.

2696
01:58:10.050 --> 01:58:10.883
I remember that.

2697
01:58:10.883 --> 01:58:12.314
Do you remember that?

2698
01:58:12.314 --> 01:58:13.764
Yeah, it was very haunting.

2699
01:58:14.870 --> 01:58:16.580
I have another, well it's too late.

2700
01:58:16.580 --> 01:58:18.460
We've already talked about that's we're moving on.

2701
01:58:18.460 --> 01:58:19.390
We're getting into some really

2702
01:58:19.390 --> 01:58:20.943
uplifting stuff like sobriety.

2703
01:58:21.950 --> 01:58:24.823
All right, Nathan from Boston.

2704
01:58:25.970 --> 01:58:26.940
Hi, Rich and Adam.

2705
01:58:26.940 --> 01:58:30.720
This is Nathan from Boston area.

2706
01:58:30.720 --> 01:58:32.770
So I have four months

2707
01:58:32.770 --> 01:58:37.180
before I'm going to be admitted to a 30-day program.

2708
01:58:37.180 --> 01:58:38.210
That's a joint program

2709
01:58:38.210 --> 01:58:41.840
for alcoholism, and anxiety and depression.

2710
01:58:41.840 --> 01:58:45.550
So my question is this, what advice would you give somebody

2711
01:58:45.550 --> 01:58:47.610
that knows they need recovery?

2712
01:58:47.610 --> 01:58:51.840
My friend and my wife have posed this to me

2713
01:58:51.840 --> 01:58:55.970
and I'm accepting it, but I have four months before I go in.

2714
01:58:55.970 --> 01:58:57.350
And during that four months,

2715
01:58:57.350 --> 01:59:01.490
I'm starting to wax and wane between completely sobering up

2716
01:59:01.490 --> 01:59:06.490
and going in as a sober person or giving up

2717
01:59:06.545 --> 01:59:10.390
and just, I almost said enjoying the next four months,

2718
01:59:10.390 --> 01:59:12.320
but you know what I mean.

2719
01:59:12.320 --> 01:59:16.210
Spiritually, pragmatically, cognitively,

2720
01:59:16.210 --> 01:59:18.332
like I'm struggling on so many levels

2721
01:59:18.332 --> 01:59:21.610
of how to deal with the next four months.

2722
01:59:21.610 --> 01:59:23.337
And I wanna make the best

2723
01:59:23.337 --> 01:59:27.080
of the situation, but it's getting difficult.

2724
01:59:27.080 --> 01:59:30.950
And so any advice you have is greatly appreciated.

2725
01:59:30.950 --> 01:59:32.550
Thank you, bye.

2726
01:59:32.550 --> 01:59:37.060
Nathan, I would say that you are suffering

2727
01:59:37.060 --> 01:59:40.290
from the alcoholic's paradox, right?

2728
01:59:40.290 --> 01:59:45.290
Like it's the two wolves, right?

2729
01:59:46.150 --> 01:59:47.560
Like which wolf do you feed?

2730
01:59:47.560 --> 01:59:52.260
So on the one hand, listen you know you need to get sober.

2731
01:59:52.260 --> 01:59:56.390
You've been intervened on, your friends are telling you,

2732
01:59:56.390 --> 01:59:59.640
you've got to go, you've relented to this intervention

2733
01:59:59.640 --> 02:00:02.700
and agreed to go to this treatment center for 30 days.

2734
02:00:02.700 --> 02:00:05.190
It's not come coming up for four months.

2735
02:00:05.190 --> 02:00:08.040
So the good devil's like, well, you should get sober now.

2736
02:00:08.040 --> 02:00:09.680
And then when you go get into treatment,

2737
02:00:09.680 --> 02:00:12.440
you can really, hit the accelerator

2738
02:00:12.440 --> 02:00:14.960
and create this amazing foundation of sobriety.

2739
02:00:14.960 --> 02:00:17.770
But the alcoholic is like, I got four months.

2740
02:00:17.770 --> 02:00:18.603
Yeah, four good months.

2741
02:00:18.603 --> 02:00:19.436
It's party time.

2742
02:00:19.436 --> 02:00:22.750
Like it's time to really accelerate this thing, right?

2743
02:00:22.750 --> 02:00:24.603
And I get that, I understand that like,

2744
02:00:24.603 --> 02:00:26.950
look, I'm going to treatment in four months.

2745
02:00:26.950 --> 02:00:28.890
I might as well go out with a bang.

2746
02:00:28.890 --> 02:00:30.260
Well don't a lot of people get high

2747
02:00:30.260 --> 02:00:31.390
the night before they check in?

2748
02:00:31.390 --> 02:00:32.490
Dude, I did, I showed up

2749
02:00:32.490 --> 02:00:35.600
on the doorstep of my treatment center completely loaded.

2750
02:00:35.600 --> 02:00:38.380
Like I tried to make the most out of that last day.

2751
02:00:38.380 --> 02:00:39.830
I'm not recommending that.

2752
02:00:39.830 --> 02:00:40.663
No.

2753
02:00:40.663 --> 02:00:45.260
I think that Nathan has an amazing opportunity here

2754
02:00:45.260 --> 02:00:47.360
because he's got four months

2755
02:00:47.360 --> 02:00:49.210
to get sober, so that when he goes

2756
02:00:49.210 --> 02:00:51.730
to treatment, he can really unpack his shit

2757
02:00:51.730 --> 02:00:55.549
and create this amazing foundation for himself.

2758
02:00:55.549 --> 02:00:57.070
You don't have to wait

2759
02:00:57.070 --> 02:00:59.200
until treatment to focus on your sobriety.

2760
02:00:59.200 --> 02:01:02.280
It's been impressed upon you that you are an alcoholic.

2761
02:01:02.280 --> 02:01:05.800
I gather that you agree with this sentiment and

2762
02:01:07.980 --> 02:01:09.900
that elevator's going down.

2763
02:01:09.900 --> 02:01:12.830
And there's no guarantee that if you decide to drink

2764
02:01:12.830 --> 02:01:16.070
or use tonight, that you're gonna wake up the next day,

2765
02:01:16.070 --> 02:01:18.200
you could get into a car wreck, you could kill somebody,

2766
02:01:18.200 --> 02:01:21.300
you could harm yourself, like all bets are off.

2767
02:01:21.300 --> 02:01:22.920
Every time you decide to take

2768
02:01:22.920 --> 02:01:26.920
that substance into your body, there is a good chance

2769
02:01:26.920 --> 02:01:29.160
that something terrible is gonna happen into your life.

2770
02:01:29.160 --> 02:01:30.810
And that's something that you can't control.

2771
02:01:30.810 --> 02:01:32.792
And as an alcoholic, that's part

2772
02:01:32.792 --> 02:01:35.770
of the allure, we can romanticize that.

2773
02:01:35.770 --> 02:01:38.430
But the harsh truth is that

2774
02:01:38.430 --> 02:01:42.900
you don't have the luxury of doing that anymore.

2775
02:01:42.900 --> 02:01:46.180
And I think this intervention probably has put a damper

2776
02:01:46.180 --> 02:01:48.290
on how fun that high is gonna be anyway,

2777
02:01:48.290 --> 02:01:49.880
because every time you drink

2778
02:01:49.880 --> 02:01:52.477
or use now in the back of your mind, you're like,

2779
02:01:52.477 --> 02:01:55.730
"I'm going to treatment, everybody knows I'm an alcoholic."

2780
02:01:55.730 --> 02:01:58.150
And the kind of beating up that you do.

2781
02:01:58.150 --> 02:01:59.940
Like I'm a piece of shit and all of that,

2782
02:01:59.940 --> 02:02:02.120
like why can't I stop this?

2783
02:02:02.120 --> 02:02:07.120
So congrats on agreeing to go to treatment, that's huge.

2784
02:02:07.590 --> 02:02:10.090
But I really, and you know this,

2785
02:02:10.090 --> 02:02:12.917
like I'm just reminding you of what you already know

2786
02:02:12.917 --> 02:02:17.330
that you can lean into your addiction and just say, fuck it

2787
02:02:17.330 --> 02:02:19.200
and party down until you have to go,

2788
02:02:19.200 --> 02:02:21.420
or you have this amazing opportunity

2789
02:02:21.420 --> 02:02:24.480
to start taking care of yourself right now.

2790
02:02:24.480 --> 02:02:26.950
So why would you wait until treatment

2791
02:02:26.950 --> 02:02:29.690
when you need to get sober right now?

2792
02:02:29.690 --> 02:02:31.330
You do seem to have some level

2793
02:02:31.330 --> 02:02:33.842
of willingness that you're trying to like,

2794
02:02:33.842 --> 02:02:36.683
on some level, you're looking for an excuse, right?

2795
02:02:36.683 --> 02:02:38.470
Like you need to get sober, you know

2796
02:02:38.470 --> 02:02:41.017
what to do in order to get sober, you go to an AA meeting.

2797
02:02:41.017 --> 02:02:43.300
It's sounds like he negotiated himself four months.

2798
02:02:43.300 --> 02:02:44.900
Yeah, he's trying to,

2799
02:02:44.900 --> 02:02:46.707
